      <h2>What Is NDT?</h2>
      <p>
        <strong>Newfoundland Daylight Time (NDT)</strong> is the seasonal daylight saving time zone observed in Newfoundland during the spring, summer, and early autumn months.
      </p>
      <p>
        NDT operates at <strong>UTC−2:30</strong> (Coordinated Universal Time minus 2 hours and 30 minutes). Clocks in Newfoundland advance 1 hour forward from NST (UTC−3:30) to NDT (UTC−2:30) on the second Sunday in March and return to NST on the first Sunday in November.
      </p>
    </section>

